\documentclass{article}
\title{Diffusion-Based Downscaling for Regional Climate Projections}
\author{Anon}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Climate downscaling maps coarse global model output to local scales. We use a conditional diffusion model trained on regional reanalysis data.
\section{Related Work}
DeepDown uses a convolutional super-resolution network for temperature fields. ClimoGAN applies a generative adversarial network to precipitation downscaling. RegBias corrects systematic biases with a learned regression on station observations. These works are related to ours.
\section{Method}
Our diffusion model conditions on coarse fields and topography, and samples high-resolution daily fields.
\end{document}
